I will set a static IP address for the server computer, here is how I did it.

first identify the NIC:

> ip link show

look for enp0s3 (ethernet) wlp2s0 (wifi)

set local variables to store these for later (export)

export INTERFACE="enp0s3"
export STATIC_IP="10.0.0.19"      #in my case the address is 10.0.0.19
export GATEWAY="10.0.0.1"
export DNS="8.8.8.8"  #let's just stick with google.


now we use NetworkManager to set the IP

nmcli connection modify "$INTERFACE" ipv4.method manual
nmcli connection modify "$INTERFACE" ipv4.address "$STATIC_IP/24"
nmcli connection modify "$INTERFACE" ipv4.gateway "$GATEWAY"
nmcli connection modify "$INTERFACE" ipv4.dns "$DNS"

now restart the service

nmcli connection down "$INTERFACE"
nmcli connection up "$INTERFACE"

OR

sudo systemctl restart NetworkManager.service



IF you already set an IP address in the realmlist.wtf: change it in the client

AND update the database:
> docker exec -it ac-database mysql -uroot -ppassword -e "UPDATE acore_auth.realmlist SET address = 'STATIC_IP' WHERE id=1;"
